# Shadcn/ui & Clean Styling Rules

## Core Principles
- **Prefer shadcn/ui**: Always check if a component exists in `@/components/ui` before creating a new one or using a third-party library.
- **No External Styles**: Do not add external CSS files, `<style>` blocks, or inline `style={{...}}` attributes to shadcn components.
- **Tailwind Only**: Use exclusively Tailwind CSS utility classes for any layout or style adjustments.

## Implementation Details
- **Atomic Changes**: When modifying shadcn components, apply Tailwind classes directly to the existing `className` props via `cn()`.
- **Consistency**: Maintain the existing design tokens (colors, radii, fonts) defined in `globals.css` and `tailwind.config.js`.
- **New Components**: If a required component is not in `ui`, build it using Radix UI primitives and Tailwind, following the shadcn pattern.

## Guidelines
- If I ask for a UI element, first suggest the shadcn version.
- Never "fix" styling by adding custom CSS classes in a global stylesheet.
- Keep the components accessible and functional as per Radix UI standards.
